===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|en|enm|smoked}}, {{m|enm|y-smoked}}, equivalent to {{af|en|smoke|-ed}}.

====Adjective====
{{en-adj|-}}

# Of food, [[preserve]]d by treatment with [[smoke]].
#: {{ux|en|'''smoked''' salmon}}
# Of glass, [[tinted]].
#* '''1908''', {{w|G. K. Chesterton}}, ''The Man who was Thursday''
#*: 'A pair of '''smoked''' spectacles will do it,' he said positively. 'Look at him now; he looks like an angelic office boy. Put him on a pair of smoked spectacles, and children will scream at the sight of him.'

